'''Mirrored''' is a special property that appear on items created by a {{il|Mirror of Kalandra}} or a {{il|Reflecting Mist}} on a piece of equipment.

Regular mirrored items always have stats and modifiers identical to the original item, and 2D art which has been flipped horizontally.

Mirrored items cannot be altered in any way except through the use of currency items that explicitly affect mirrored items, such as {{il|Reflective Oil}}.

==Reflected items==
The [[Lake Islet]] [[Atlas anomaly]] contains a [[Reflecting Mist (interactable object)|Reflecting Mist]] interactable. Interacting with it can open a menu that offers you a choice between two Reflected mirrored Rare [[ring]]s or [[amulet]]s with unusual explicit mods. Some are scaled-up versions of existing modifiers, while others are strong negative versions of the same modifier. The rings provide inverse stats; a negative mod on one ring is positive on the other. You may only pick one of these items to take.

Rarely, the Reflecting Mist will drop an [[Reflecting Mist|itemized]] version of itself, allowing the player to reflect their own Rare ring or amulet.

==Trivia==
It may be implied that [[Unique item]]s obtained by players are actually Mirrored versions of the original items, and why Unique items cannot be mirrored. Former developer, Qarl, said that Hyrri has the original {{il|Hyrri's Ire}}, but its 3D art is mirrored compared to the player obtainable version.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/37819/page/4#p521723|title=Re: A selection from my PoE pictures folder, including beta nostalgia|date=July 11, 2012|accessdate=October 7, 2022|publisher-Official Path of Exile Forums}}</ref>{{speculation}}

==Version history==
